{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvazCQrQDoSAdcpr6NJB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**My recommendation: don't treat the result as a pricing problem, and don't let a non-buyer survey decide this.**\n\n**What the numbers say:**\n- 0.3% of 20,000 is about 60 buyers. About 24 asked for refunds, so roughly 36 kept it. That's 0.18% net, or about £540 a month.\n- The target was 3%. Net take-up is more than 16 times short. A price cut almost never closes a gap that large. Even at £5, you'd need roughly ten times the demand just to match the revenue you have now.\n- A 40% refund rate is the bigger warning. The people who wanted it most tried it and many found it wasn't worth £15. That points to a problem with the product or how it was described, not the price. Cutting the price doesn't fix that.\n\n**Why the survey is the wrong tool:**\n- What people say they'd pay is a poor guide to what they actually pay. People who didn't buy will often say \"maybe at £5\" and then still not buy.\n- It asks people who didn't buy about price, when the clearest evidence comes from those who bought and asked for refunds.\n\n**What to do instead:**\n1. **Talk to the refunders.** There are only about 24, so you can interview them all. Did support feel no better than the free tier? Was it slow? Did the description promise something it didn't deliver?\n2. **Use the control group.** Compare churn, support contacts and satisfaction between the two groups. Showing the offer may have hurt goodwill or made the free support look worse.\n3. **Check where the 3% target came from.** If nothing backed it up, reset it.\n4. **Make the decision.** Shelve the add-on at £15. Only test a different price if step 1 shows a value problem you can fix. If you do, run it as a randomised price test, not a survey.\n\nOne caution: 60 buyers is a small sample, so the refund rate is imprecise. But the shortfall in take-up is far too large to be noise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3190,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3190},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed6744ac-82f4-46b3-8139-a361f1b59d8b","uuid":"1e161ac1-a02e-44ea-b506-d5f3b7772e56","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:12:49.142Z","request_id":"req_011CfvazC2nVEsUm6kvCfA5K"}
